# Orchestrator cheap-helper rule

Applies only to the Project **orchestrator** (cursor-001, frontier model). Workers and helpers ignore this rule.

Do not use the frontier model for everything. It is for thinking-heavy work. Hand well-defined routine jobs to a cheap cursor-001 subagent.

## Stays on the frontier model

- Planning: splitting intent into Phases and Issues, wave and dependency order.
- Writing Issue briefs detailed enough for a mid-level model.
- Judgement reviews: is the work correct, complete, in scope; is a design sound.
- Decisions: merge or not, repair-ladder escalation, routing, anything recorded as a Ledger decision.
- Talking to Carlos: questions (one at a time, multiple choice, with a recommendation) and plain-language summaries of outcomes.
- Handling security findings, secrets and credentials.

## Goes to a cheap helper

- Lookups: find files, symbols, config values, repo facts, CI or PR status details.
- Reading and writing company memory (LiNKbrain via the hub) and LiNKskills lookups.
- Research and collecting sources.
- Summaries: logs, diffs, long docs, worker lessons notes (distil into Brain findings).
- Mechanical checks: run fast checks and report results, validate files against a schema, compare lists.
- Drafting routine text the frontier model then approves (Phase Issue tables, changelog lines).

Models, in order: `grok-4.7` medium, then `composer-2.5`. Resolve the exact slug from the available model list at hand-off time.

## Not helper work either

- **Issue coding** always goes to Codex CLI (Luna High / Sol Medium) or cursor-002 (Grok 4.7 Medium / Opus 5.5 Medium) per the routing rules, never to a cursor-001 helper and never to the orchestrator itself.
- **One-command jobs** (a single `git`, `gh`, run-log or watchdog command) are run directly; spawning a helper costs more than it saves.

## How to hand off

- Give a self-contained brief: goal, exact paths or IDs, read-only unless writing is the job, and the exact return format.
- Ask for facts with sources (path, line, URL), not opinions.
- Run independent helper jobs in parallel.
- Spot-check any helper result that feeds a decision. If a helper fails or is ambiguous twice, do the job on the frontier model and note it.
- Helpers never merge, promote, write the Ledger, message Carlos, or change external systems.
